infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Two non-atomic steps, two orderings — only one is safe
  desc The relay must publish to the broker AND mark the row sent. The order it does them in decides whether a crash leaves a duplicate or a lost event.
  compares
    - label Publish, then mark sent
      children
        - label Crash gap → duplicate
          desc Broker accepted the message but the UPDATE never committed; the row still looks unsent, so restart republishes it
        - label At-least-once delivery
          desc Every event arrives one or more times — never zero
        - label Recoverable
          desc An idempotent consumer dedupes on the event id, so a re-fire is harmless
        - label The chosen ordering
          desc Pairs with an inbox table or a unique constraint on the side effect
    - label Mark sent, then publish
      children
        - label Crash gap → lost event
          desc UPDATE committed but the publish never happened; the row looks done while nothing was sent
        - label At-most-once delivery
          desc An event can silently arrive zero times — the original dual-write bug returns
        - label Unrecoverable
          desc No downstream signal exists to detect or replay the event that vanished
        - label Rejected
          desc Moves the gap without closing it — strictly worse than a duplicate
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
